- op: discuss  # 5e61
  at: '2026-09-19T23:41:11Z'  # 5e61
  by: agent  # 5e61
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5e61
  clock: 3  # 5e61
  nonce: '5e61'  # 5e61
  message: "Satisfied. The audit this row asked for is done, and the verdict differs per attribute.\n\n**`Edge.confidence` — NOT the defect, with positive evidence.** `Edge.create` always computes a value: an explicit producer constant, a value DERIVED from the pathway, or the unseeded 0.85 fallback — and it stamps `confidence_source` (`evidence_derived` / `emitter_constant`) to say which. Measured on the 207,779 edges of this repository's own survey: **zero** edges carry the fallback. The 157 `emitter_constant` edges whose pathway is unseeded all carry explicit constants (0.9 x82, 0.7 x63, 0.9 x8, 0.95 x3, 0.75 x1). No producer abstains on confidence, so the merge pass's candidate set cannot contain an unobserved one. The dataclass default 0.85 is unreachable through the emission surface.\n\n**`Edge.evidence_type` — the defect, and worse than this row assumed.** I filed it as a possible phantom. It is a false POSITIVE claim. The default is `ast_call_direct`, the most specific pathway in a 126-value vocabulary, so a producer that omits the keyword does not abstain — it asserts a direct call site it never saw. **51 sites did** (AST enumeration over `packages/*/src`), including:\n- `linkers/route_handler.py` x2 — a route->handler dispatch linker that reads no call site at all (15 such edges on the self-corpus);\n- `proto.py` / `thrift.py` / `capnp.py` — `contains` edges for a declaration nested in its parent;\n- five build-manifest `defines_target` declarations (`json_config.py`, `manifest_targets.py`, `xml_config.py`);\n- `cli.py`'s hand-rolled behavior-map deserializer, which also dropped `meta`, `is_resolved`, `dst_ref` and `confidence_source` on every reconstructed edge.\nAnd it compounds: `Edge.create` DERIVES confidence from `evidence_type` and then stamps the result `evidence_derived`, so a defaulted pathway fabricates a derived confidence with provenance attached. ADR-0057 §13's corroboration rule keys on the same field — two DISTINCT `evidence_type`s make a folded edge corroborated at 0.95 — so a defaulted value can manufacture or mask corroboration.\n\n**THE CURE, following INV-kubup's precedent: make the omission impossible rather than detect the phantom.** All 51 sites now name their pathway, each chosen from the canonical `inference_pathway` axis against what the site actually reads — `ast_import` / `import_declaration` / `include` for import constructs, `ast_call` (`ast_call_direct` only for a bare-name local call) for call expressions, `enclosing_scope` for declaration nesting, `reference` for a resolved name reference, `build_dependency` / `build_target_main` for build declarations, `source_statement` for a `source`, `naming_convention` for Go's build-tag alternatives, `dispatch_pattern` for the route linker. `cli.py` now uses `Edge.from_dict` — the one deserializer, which reads `meta.evidence_type` back.\n\n**THE GATE:** `producer_coherence.edge_sites_without_evidence_type`, wired into the L3 producer-coherence linter (pre-commit + CI) beside the existing unregistered-value ratchet. A new `Edge` / `Edge.create` under the producer roots that does not name its pathway fails the build. `**kwargs` forwarding is not reported (it cannot be read statically) and tests are excluded, as for the sibling registry checks.\n\n**EVIDENCE.** Live tree: 51 -> 0 sites. Mutation: removing one site's declaration turns the gate test red AND fails the linter by name (2 failed). Four synthetic tests pin the finder's behaviour in both directions (reported / not reported / kwargs / tests / unparseable). Artifact, before vs after on the same repository: 16 edges changed their declared pathway — 15 route-handler dispatches from `ast_call_direct` to `dispatch_pattern`, one `contains` to `enclosing_scope` — and one edge's confidence moved 0.85 -> 0.9 as a consequence. The number is small **because this corpus contains almost none of the affected languages** (ada, agda, capnp, circom, d, fish, gdscript, lean, nim, solidity, tlaplus, thrift, proto, starlark, powershell, asm); for those the correctness of each value rests on the site's own reading, which is why every one was chosen against the construct the code matches rather than by pattern. The full 498-file affected slice passes and every changed file is at 100%.\n\n**WORTH SAYING PLAINLY:** not one existing test went red when I changed 50 producer sites. The false claim was never pinned by anything — which is how it survived. The route-handler pathway is now pinned in its linker's own test, and the gate is what covers the rest."  # 5e61
